  "title": "Room Acoustical Parameters as Predictors of Acoustic Comfort in Outdoor Spaces of Housing Complexes",
  "authors": "Armin Taghipour et al., 2020",
  "research_question": "To what extent classic room acoustical parameters (STI, D50, C50, C80, EDT, LF80, EchoD) and A-weighted equivalent continuous sound level (LAeq) are able to predict perceived short-term acoustic comfort in outdoor spaces (i.e., courtyards) of virtual housing complexes, considering the effects of facade absorption, sound source, and observer position.",
  "design_type": "within_subjects|mixed_factorial",
  "participants": {
    "n": 69,
    "description": "Experiment 1: 27 subjects (7 females, 20 males, aged 19-57, median 38). Experiments 2 & 3: 42 subjects (13 females, 29 males, aged 18-64, median 41). All self-reported normal-hearing.",
    "recruitment": "Most subjects worked for the authors' research institute."
  },
  "stimuli_or_exposures": [
    {
      "type": "audio",
      "description": "Auralized stimuli from virtual inner yards (100x20x20m, unceiled, brick/concrete walls with glass windows) with varied facade absorption (reflecting, absorbing, exaggerated absorption, aw values 0.05, 0.15, 0.30, 0.55, 0.95) and balcony ceiling absorption (aw values 0.05, 0.30, 0.95). Sound sources included bouncing basketball, doll's pram, German conversation, children playing, crying baby, Swiss German conversation. Stimuli were 8-10s long, normalized to LAeq of 50 dB(A) for ODEON input. Played back via 2D surround sound over 5 loudspeakers and 2 subwoofers.",
      "n_stimuli": 127,
      "source": "Figure 4, Section 2.3, 3.1, 3.2, 3.3"
    }
  ],
  "measures": [
